## OAuth2 Authentication Implementation Details

### OAuth2 Flow Setup
1. Register your application with Google Cloud Console to obtain client credentials
2. Implement the following OAuth2 endpoints:
   - Authorization endpoint: `https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth`
   - Token endpoint: `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`
   - Scopes needed: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/presentations`, `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly`

### Node.js Implementation
```javascript
const {google} = require('googleapis');

// OAuth2 configuration
const oauth2Client = new google.auth.OAuth2(
  process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
  process.env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
  process.env.GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI
);

// Generate authorization URL
function getAuthorizationUrl() {
  return oauth2Client.generateAuthUrl({
    access_type: 'offline',
    scope: [
      'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/presentations',
      'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly'
    ],
    prompt: 'consent' // Force to get refresh token
  });
}

// Exchange authorization code for tokens
async function getAccessToken(code) {
  try {
    const {tokens} = await oauth2Client.getToken(code);
    oauth2Client.setCredentials(tokens);
    return tokens;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error exchanging code for token:', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

### Token Management
1. Store access tokens securely in database with user association
2. Implement token refresh logic when tokens expire
3. Include proper error handling for authentication failures

### Security Considerations
- Use HTTPS for all OAuth2 redirects and API calls
- Implement state parameter for CSRF protection
- Store client secret securely using environment variables
- Validate all OAuth responses before processing
